data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"researcher","content":"- CRISPR gene editing is a genetic engineering technique that modifies the genomes of living organisms, based on a simplified bacterial CRISPR-Cas9 antiviral defense system [1].\n- Cas9 nuclease, complexed with a synthetic guide RNA (gRNA) and delivered into a cell, can cut the genome at a desired location [1].\n- Genome editing targets insertions to site-specific locations, unlike early methods that inserted genetic material randomly [3].\n- Programmable \"molecular scissors\" such as restriction endonucleases create double-strand breaks in DNA [3]."}

